refactor: the shelf's outlines onto page.html's node, python first

want
  One outline, many components. The outline is fixed: nodes, folds, keys, find,
  address. What a node draws is a component's own. Python is the first
  component, and the one that was too noisy: a ringed bullet per def, its
  whole signature the heading, every row one weight.

the node (page.html's, kept as is)

    details#id                  id is the address, and what makes it a node
      summary
        heading                 first child: the text find and the box list
        edge ...                the rest: figures, a glyph, a count
      body                      a component: anything with no details#id in it

  look comes from nesting alone: a node holding nodes is a card, one holding
  none a row. Do not style it again. A component may keep its own markup in
  body and in the edge; it may not put a details#id there, or the keys walk in.

the case, carried through
  proj/poc/model.py. Field.broken_constraint:

    heading   def broken_constraint(value)          faint def, bold name
    edge      [skyline glyph]  29
    body      206..225, the source as written, line numbers kept, strings
              faded

decided
  node       page.html's, frozen. The checker is the oracle.
  python row the def line itself, no pill: `@property def parts()`,
             `@dataclass class Field`, `class Request(Base)`. def is
             faint and means a plain method; a class says class once, as a
             card. self and cls dropped; a default over 10 chars is =...
             Hover: the full signature and the docstring. The docstring line
             is not a row. Kind is a word in the code, not a pill and not a
             glyph column.
  edge       skyline glyph (one bar per line, height the indent, 90x16) and the
             size. Nothing else, no bars.
  body       opens at the first line after the def line, docstring and all,
             as written (numbered, strings quiet). The lines between a
             body's classes and defs (imports, constants, fields, comments)
             show as source, in file order. A module's docstring is the
             lead, kept as written (pre-wrap, mono).
  strings    quiet: string literals faint, comments italic and faint. Keywords
             if elif else for while try except finally with return raise break
             continue yield bold, one style, no tints.
  folds      none: a page hides nothing. A def of any size is a node, so a
             2-line __init__ opens; a class's fields show as source, not a
             count.
  rail       none: the bars, ticks, arcs, return/raise/jump marks and the
             legend did not help reading; the code does.
  ids        qualified name: Field.broken_constraint

not taken, and why
  structogram, skeleton, exits table   hide code the reader wants whole
  treemap, call graph, matrix, arcs,   a second structure beside the outline;
  scatter, data cards, class cards     good as a separate view, not the outline
  signature as heading                 the how fills the line, the what is lost
  pill on every row, glyph column      noise; no mark is the default
  d3, dagre, mermaid, graphviz         shelf is one file; none was needed
  Prior art, for the record: Code::Blocks NassiShneiderman and
  create-struktex draw structograms from c and java; `CodeVisualizer`
  and `Function Graph Overview` draw a flowchart per function; none
  draws the code with a rail. Shneiderman's 1982 experiments found data
  structure info helped more than control flow.

order
  1  node contract, md only. ids on details; keyed() takes details[id]; heading
     = first child; edge slot; body in a div; the page.html look from nesting.
     Smallest step, every kind rides it. Shelf's checker stays green, and an
     md file's keys behave as page/run.mjs says.
  2  node shape {id, heading, edge[], body} in sections() and defs(); part()
     builds from it. Diff takes its edge (M +n -m) here.
  3  python heading: kind, name, params, from the signature lines defs()
     already joins; drop self/cls, shorten defaults.
  4  python edge: the skyline from indent per line.
  5  python folds: record fields and small defs as group nodes.
  6  python body: first statement, line numbers, quiet strings, then the rail.
     4 to 6 moved to medium/page/py: a page of its own, made from the ast as
     page/diff is. The shelf does not call it yet.
  7  retire the ring and guide css for python.
  Built: 1 to 3 in the shelf (`medium/shelf/run.mjs:/refactor, step 1/`),
  4 and 6 in page/py, without the rail; 5 is dropped, for a page hides
  nothing. Open: 7, for the shelf still rings a folded bullet
  (`medium/shelf.html:/wears a ring/`).

check
  1  node medium/shelf/run.mjs                      green before and after
  2  md: a file with a duplicate heading, a fenced block holding #, a setext
